.TH "main_wrapper" "3head" "2026\-10\-05" "TheCRatTime" "atexit"
.SH NAME
\fBmain_wrapper.\&h\fR \- generate wrapper for function \fBmain\fR.\&
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
See \fBgen_wrapper\fR(3head).\&
.PP
This is pre\-generated wrapper for main, you need define one macro
instead of four.\&
.PP
\fBMAIN_VOID\fR
.RS 4
Without arguments exclude first \fBAtExitHeader\fR.\&
.RE
.PP
\fBMAIN_ARGV\fR
.RS 4
Three arguments: \fBAtExitHeader\fR, \fBint argc\fR and \fBchar** argv\fR.\&
.RE
.PP
\fBMAIN_ENVP\fR
.RS 4
Four arguments: \fBAtExitHeader\fR, \fBint argc\fR, \fBchar** argv\fR and \fBchar** envp\fR.\&
.RE
.PP

You also can define \fBATEXIT_DIS_ERROR\fR.
.PP
You can define \fBNO_UNDEFS\fR and \fBMAIN_*\fR macro don't will be
undefined by \fB#undef\fR.\&
.PP
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
/* void main */
#define MAIN_VOID
#include "main_wrapper.h"
#include <atexit.h>

/* Real main function: */
int Main(AtExitHeader* main_atexit) {
  /* ... */
  return 0;
}
.fi
.PP
.SH AUTHORS
Project and man\-page: TheCRatTime
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBatexit_do\fR(3), \fBSetAtExit\fR(3), \fBgen_wrapper\fR(3head), \fBAtExitHeader\fR(3type)
